{"availability":"available","full":"akareiko/coupnii","name":"coupnii","description":"Custom demo/playground on niivue-react (medical image viewer) with my own MRI data. Core library is upstream, not original.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2024-10-31T09:15:14Z","updated":"2026-09-10T07:02:53Z","license":"BSD-2-Clause","branch":"main","homepage":"https://coupnii.vercel.app","topics":["medical-imaging","react"],"demo":"https://coupnii.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T03:01:18.892Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T03:01:18.892Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T03:01:18.892Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T22:39:59.975Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-18T03:01:18.892Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A customized playground built on top of niivue-react, an open-source React wrapper around Niivue (a WebGL medical image viewer). The core library (src/) is the upstream niivue-react package, unmodified; what's mine is the example app in examples/ — a custom viewer wired up to my own MRI/segmentation data instead of the library's demo dataset, used to explore rendering aligned and segmented brain volumes side by side.","This sits alongside coupdegrace, a from-scratch medical imaging upload/visualization tool — this repo is a smaller, separate exploration of Niivue's React bindings rather than part of that project."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/akareiko/coupnii/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"122e9af8ac5c8925fe54a8168f2b842203495bfd4b3949f12b3afd69c7372146","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:00.133Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:00.133Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A customized playground built on top of niivue-react, an open-source React wrapper around Niivue (a WebGL medical image viewer). The core library (src/) is the upstream niivue-react package, unmodifie